    "q": "When pure NOCl gas is heated to a certain temperature in a 1L-closed container it decomposes according to the equation 2NOCl(g) ⇌ 2NO(g) + Cl2{(g) and when the reaction reached equilibrium it was found that total pressure of equilibrium mixture equal 1 atm and the partial pressure of NOCl equal 0.4 atm calculate:\n1) the partial pressure of NOCl before decomposition .\n2) equilibrium constant Kp at the same temperature .\n(3 د 2020 )\nSol\nبما انه ذكر في السؤال كلمة ( found ) اذأ نقوم بكتابة الفرضية\n[TABLE]\nنطبق dalton law for parital pressures الذي ينص على :\nThe total pressure is equal to the sum of the parital pressures of gases in the mixture .\nPT = PNOCl + PNO + PCl2\n1 = 0.4 + 2X + X ⇒ 1 = 0.4 + 3X\n3 X = 1 - 0.4 ⇒ 3X = 0.6\nX = (0.6)/(3) ⇒ X = 0.2 atm\nA - 2X = 0.4 ⇒ A - 2(0.2) = 0.4\nA - 0.4 = 0.4 ⇒ A = 0.4 + 0.4\nPartial pressure of NOCl before decomposition\nA = 0.8 atm\nPNO = 2X = 2(0.2) ⇒ PNO = 0.4 atm\nPCl2 = X ⇒ PCl2 = 0.2 atm\nKp = P^2NO × PCl2{P^2NOCl\nKp = ((0.4)^2 (0.2))/((0.4)^2)\nKp = 0.2",
    "a": "(See solution in original Ministry exam.)"
