    "q": "When NOCl gas is heated in 1L closed container it decomposes according to the following equation 2NOCl ⇌ 2NO + Cl2 and when the reaction reaches equilibrium it was found that the total pressure of equilibrium mixture equal 6atm and partial pressure of NOCl at equilibrium equal 3atm calculate:\n1-partial pressure of NOCl gas before decomposition .\n2- the equilibrium constant Kp at same temperature .\n(2 د 2018 )\nSol\nبما انه في السؤال كلمة ( found ) اذأ نقوم بكتابة الفرضية .\n[TABLE]\nنطبق dalton law for parital pressures : الذي ينص على :\nThe total pressure is equal to the sum of the parital pressures of gases in the mixture\nPT = PNOCl + PNO + PCl2\n6 = 3 + 2X + X ⇒ 6 = 3 + 3X\n3 X = 6 - 3 ⇒ 3X = 3\nX = (3)/(3) ⇒ X = 1 atm\nA - 2X = 3 ⇒ A - 2(1) = 3\nA - 2 = 3 ⇒ A = 3 + 2\nPartial pressure of NOCl before decomposition\nA = 5 atm\nPNO = 2X = 2(1) ⇒ PNO = 2 atm\nPCl2 = X ⇒ PCl2 = 1 atm\nKp = P^2NO × PCl2{P^2NOCl\nKp = ((2)^2 (1))/((3)^2) = (4)/(9) ⇒ Kp = 0.444\nالفصل الثاني\nالكيمياء I\nوزارة 27",
