    "q": "As a result of reaction of CO gas with water vapor in a 1-litter closed container at 700K, CO2 and H2 gases where formed . What is the concentration of gas mixture at equilibrium if 1mole of each of reactant and products where placed as Kc = 5.29 ? √(5.29) = 2.3. (2018 ت)\nSol since the volume equal 1L then n = M\nبما انه تم وضع مول واحد من كل من المتفاعلات والنواتج اذا لا يمكن ان نكتب الفرضية لأننا لا نعرف اتجاه التفاعل ..... اذا يجب ان نستخرج Q ونقارن مع Kc لمعرفة اتجاه التفاعل\nالتراكيز الابتدائية\nCO(g) + H2O(g) ⇌ CO2(g) + H2(g)\n1 ...... 1 1 nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; nbsp; 1\nQ = ([CO2][H2])/([CO][H2O]) = ((1)(1))/((1)(1)) = 1\nWe note that Kc > Q so the direction of the reaction is forward that is in the product +x and in the reactant -x\nنكتب الفرضية\n[TABLE]\nKc = ([CO2][H2])/([CO][H2O]) ⇒ 5.29 = ([1 + X]^2)/([1 - X]^2) \nوسطين × طرفين\n2.3 = (1 + X)/(1 - X)\n2.3(1 - X) = 1 + X ⇒ 2.3 - 2.3X = 1 + X\n2.3X + X = 2.3 - 1\n3.3X = 1.3 ⇒ X = (1.3)/(3.3) ⇒ X = 0.393M\nنعوض قيمة X في الخطوة الثالثة (equilibrium state) لمعرفة concentrations at equilibrium\n[CO] = [H2O] = 1 - X\n[CO] = [H2O] = 1 - 0.393\n[CO] = [H2O] = 0.607M\n[CO2] = [H2] = 1 + X\n[CO2] = [H2] = 1 + 0.393\n[CO2] = [H2] = 1.393M\nالاتزان الكيميائي HUSSIEN AL HASHEMI\n**28**",
    "a": "(See solution in original Ministry exam.)"
