    "q": "Sol\nfor equilibrium gaseous reaction 2SO3 ⇌ 2SO2 + O2 the Equilibrium mixture at 27°C contains 0.003M of SO3, 0.06M of SO2 and 0.02M of O2 when cooling the reaction to 12°C it was found that Kc = 2, is the reaction endothermic or exothermic? ( 1د2016 )\nمن خلال molar concentrations نستخرج Kc عند 25C°\n2SO3(g) ⇌ 2SO2(g) + O2(g)\n0.003 0.06 0.02\nKc = [SO2]² [O2] / [SO3]²\nKc = (0.06)²(0.02) / (0.003)² = 0.000072 / 0.000009 = 8\nالان نقارن قيم Kc مع درجات الحرارة\n[TABLE]\nWhen the temperature decrease the value of equilibrium constant kc decrease this mean the reaction is endothermic.",
