    "q": "In the following equilibrium reaction 2SO3 ⇌ 2SO2 + O2 It was found that the equilibrium mixture at 25^ C contains [SO3] = 0.002M, [SO2] = 0.08M and [O2] = 0.01 M. when the reaction is cooled to 7^ C, it was found that Kc = 5.6 then tell if the reaction is an endothermic or an exothermic one . (ت 2020)\nSol\nنستخرج Kc عند 25^ C\n2SO3(g) ⇌ 2SO2(g) + O2(g)\n0.002 0.08 0.01\nKc = ([SO2]^2 [O2])/([SO3]^2)\nKc = ((0.08)^2(0.01))/((0.002)^2)\nKc = (0.000064)/(0.000004) = 16\nالان نقارن قيم Kc مع درجات الحرارة\n[TABLE]\nWhen the temperature decrease the value of equilibrium constant kc decrease this mean the reaction is endothermic.",
    "a": "(See solution in original Ministry exam.)"
